          "filename": "Burrator Reservoir Dam Face, Dartmoor - geograph.org.uk - 1067518.jpg",
          "caption": "Burrator Reservoir Dam Face, Dartmoor Work started on the Dam on August 9th 1893 and it was opened in 1898.  The dam cost £102,000. The dam is built across the river Meavy at the Burrator Gorge.  It is constructed of concrete faced with dressed granite. The height of the dam was raised by 10ft in 1923 to increase capacity to 1,000 million gallons. The area of the reservoir is approximately 150 acres.",
